    "rs|RS248_2019-02-08|english": "V ol. 248 Friday\nNo. 7 8 February, 2019\n 19 Magha, 1940 (Saka)\nPARLIAMENTARY DEBATES\nRAJYA SABHA\nOFFICIAL REPORT\n(EN gLISH  VERSION)\nCONTENTS\nPapers laid on the Table (pages 1-6)\nReports of the Committee on Papers Laid on the Table  — Presented (page 6)\nInformation of the House (page 7-8)\n©\nRAJYA SABHA SECRETARIAT\nNEW DELHI\nPrice  : ` 100.00\n\n Website : http://rajyasabha.nic.in\n\t \t \t http://parliamentofindia.nic.in\n E-mail : rs-engdebate@sansad.nic.in\n\nRAJYA SABHA\nFriday, the 8th February, 2019/19 Magha, 1940 (Saka)\nThe House met at eleven of the clock,  \nMR. CHAIRMAN  in the Chair.\nPAPERS LAID ON THE TABLE\nNotifications of the Ministry of Consumer Affairs, Food and Public Distribution\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF CONSUMER AFFAIRS, \nFOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION; AND THE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE \nMINISTRY OF COMMERCE AND INDUSTRY (SHRI C.R. CHAUDHARY): Sir, \nI lay on the Table, under Section 7 of the Aadhaar (Targeted Delivery of Financial \nand Other Subsidies, Benefits and Services) Act, 2016, a copy each (in English and \nHindi) of the following Notifications of the Ministry of Consumer Affairs, Food and \nPublic Distribution (Department of Food and Public Distribution):—\n(1) S.O. 4998 (E), dated the 27th September, 2018, amending Notification No. \nS.O. 371 (E), dated the 8th February, 2017, to substitute certain entries in \nthe original Notification.\n(2) S.O. 6353 (E), dated the 27th October, 2018, amending Notification No. \nS.O. 371 (E), dated the 8th February, 2017, to substitute certain entries in \nthe original Notification. [Placed in Library. See No. L.T. 10782/16/19]\nReport 2017-18 of RLBCAU, Jhansi, Madhya Pradesh and related papers\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND \nFARMERS WELFARE; AND THE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF \nPANCHAYATI RAJ (SHRI PARSHOTTAM RUPALA): Sir, I lay on the Table, the \nfollowing papers:–\n(1) A copy each (in English and Hindi) of the following papers, under sub-section \n(3) of Section 30 of the Rani Lakshmi Bai Central Agricultural University \nAct, 2014:—\n(a) Annual Report of the Rani Lakshmi Bai Central Agricultural University \n(RLBCAU), Jhansi, Madhya Pradesh, for the year 2017-18.\n(b) Review by Government on the working of the above University.\n\n2 Papers laid on [RAJYA SABHA] the Table\n(2) Statement (in English and Hindi) giving reasons for the delay in laying the \npapers mentioned at (1) above.\n[Placed in Library. See No. L.T. 10912/16/19]\nI. Notifications of the Ministry of Communications\nII. Report and Accounts (2017-18) of BSNL, New Delhi and related papers\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE OF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS \nAND THE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI \nMANOJ SINHA): Sir, I laly on the Table, the following papers:–\nI. A copy each (in English and Hindi) of the following Notifications of the \nMinistry of Communications (Department of Telecommunications), under \nSection 37 of the Telecom Regulatory Authority of India Act, 1997:—\n(1) No. 116-6/2017-NSL-II, dated the 13th December, 2018, publishing the \nTelecommunication Mobile Number Portability (Seventh Amendment) \nRegulations, 2018 (9 of 2018), along with delay statement.\n(2) No. 311-04/2017-QoS, dated the 21st December, 2018, publishing the \nTelecom Commercial Communications Customer Preference (Amendment) \nRegulations, 2018 (10 of 2018), along with delay statement.\n(3) F. No. 21-04/2018-B&CS, dated the 28th December, 2018, publishing \nthe Telecommunication (Broadcasting and Cable) Services Standards \nof Quality of Service and Consumer Protection (Addressable Systems) \n(Amendment) Regulations, 2018 (11 of 2018).\n(4) No. 311-04/2017-QoS, dated the 21st December, 2018, publishing \nCorrigendum to Notification No. 311-04/2017-QoS, dated the 19th July, \n2018, along with delay statement.\n[Placed in Library. For (1) to (4) See No. L.T. 10791/16/19]\nII. (1) A copy each (in English and Hindi) of the following papers, under \nsub-section (1) (b) of Section 394 of the Companies Act, 2013:—\n(a) Eighteenth Annual Report and Accounts of the Bharat Sanchar \nNigam Limited (BSNL), New Delhi, for the year 2017-18, together \nwith the Auditor’s Report on the Accounts and the comments of \nthe Comptroller and Auditor General of India thereon.\n(b) Performance Review of the Bharat Sanchar Nigam Limited (BSNL), \nfor the year 2017-18.\n(2) Statement (in English and Hindi) giving reasons for the delay in laying \nthe papers mentioned at (1) above.\n[Placed in Library. See No. L.T. 10960/16/19]\n\nPapers laid on [8 February, 2019] the Table 3\nReports and Accounts (2017-18) of C-DAC and C-MET, Pune and related papers\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF PARLIAMENTARY \nAFFAIRS; AND THE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF STATISTICS \nAND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION (SHRI VIJAY GOEL): Sir, on behalf of \nShri S.S. Ahluwalia, I lay on the Table, a copy each (in English and Hindi) of the \nfollowing papers:—\n(i) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the Centre for Development of Advanced \nComputing (C-DAC), Pune, for the year 2017-18, together with the \nAuditor’s Report on the Accounts.\n(b) Review by Government on the working of the above Centre.\n(c) Statement giving reasons for the delay in laying the papers mentioned \nat (i) (a) above. [Placed in Library. See No. L.T. 10799/16/19]\n(ii) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the Centre for Materials for Electronics \nTechnology (C-MET), Pune, for the year 2017-18, together with the \nAuditor’s Report on the Accounts.\n(b) Review by Government on the working of the above Centre.\n(c) Statement giving reasons for the delay in laying the papers mentioned \nat (ii) (a) above. [Placed in Library. See No. L.T. 10798/16/19]\nI. Notifications of the Ministry of Railways\nII. Report and Accounts (2017-18) of HMRDC, Bengaluru and related papers\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS (SHRI RAJEN \nGOHAIN): Sir, I lay on the Table:—\nI. A copy each (in English and Hindi) of the following Notifications of the \nMinistry of Railways, under Section 199 of the Railways Act, 1989, along \nwith delay statement:—\n(1) G.S.R. 278 (E), dated the 26th March, 2018, publishing the Railways \n(Punitive charges for overloading of wagon) Amendment Rules, 2018.\n(2) G.S.R. 1205 (E), dated the 14th December, 2018, publishing the Railways \n(Punitive charges for overloading of wagon) Second Amendment Rules, \n2018. [Placed in Library. See No. L.T. 10800/16/19]\nII. (1) A copy each (in English and Hindi) of the following papers, under \nsub-section (1) (b) of Section 394 of the Companies Act, 2013:—\n(a) Fifteenth Annual Report and Accounts of the Hassan Mangalore Rail \nDevelopment Company Limited (HMRDC), Bengaluru, for the year \n2017-18, together with the Auditor’s Report on the Accounts and the \ncomments of the Comptroller and Auditor General of India thereon.\n\n4 Papers laid on [RAJYA SABHA] the Table\n(b) Review by Government on the working of the above Company.\n(2) Statement (in English and Hindi) giving reasons for the delay in laying \nthe papers mentioned at (1) above.\n[Placed in Library. See No. L.T. 10968/16/19]\nI. Notifications of the Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare\nII. Report and Accounts (2017-18) of NSC Limited, New Delhi and related \npapers\nSHRI PARSHOTTAM RUPALA: Sir, I lay on the Table, the following papers:–\nI. (A) A copy each (in English and Hindi) of the following Notifications of the \nMinistry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare (Department of Agriculture, \nCo-operation and Farmers Welfare), under sub-section (6) of Section 3 \nof the Essential Commodities Act, 1955:—\n(1) S.O. 350 (E), dated the 19th January, 2019, notifying the specifications \nof customised fertilizer, as mentioned therein, for a period of three \nyears from the date of publication of the notification in the Official \nGazette.\n(2) S.O. 351 (E), dated the 19th January, 2019, amending Notification \nNo. S.O. 3225 (E), dated the 3rd October, 2017, to substitute certain \nentries in the original Notification.\n(3) S.O. 352 (E), dated the 19th January, 2019, amending Notification \nNo. S.O. 3226 (E), dated the 3rd October, 2017, to insert certain \nentries in the original Notification.\n(4) S.O. 353 (E), dated the 19th January, 2019, notifying the specifications \nof customised fertilizer, as mentioned therein, for a period of four \nyears from the date of publication of the notification in the Official \nGazette.\n(5) S.O. 4199 (E), dated the 29th August, 2018, in supersession of \nthe Notification No. S.O. 1211 (E), dated the 19th April, 2017, \nconstituting the Central Fertiliser Committee consisting of the \nmembers as mentioned therein for a period of 5 years from the \ndate of publication of the notification in the official Gazette.\n[Placed in Library. For (1) to (5) See No. L.T. 10923/16/19]\n(B) A copy each (in English and Hindi) of the following Notifications of the \nMinistry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare (Department of Agriculture, \nCooperation and Farmers Welfare), under sub-section (3) of Section 36 \nof the Insecticides Act, 1968:—\n\nPapers laid on [8 February, 2019] the Table 5\n(1) G.S.R. 11 (E), dated the 4th January, 2019, publishing the Insecticides \n(Amendment) Rules, 2019.\n(2) G.S.R. 1204 (E), dated the 13th December, 2018, publishing the \nInsecticides (Second Amendment) Rules, 2018.\n[Placed in Library. See No. L.T. 10784/16/19]\n(C) A copy (in English and Hindi) of the Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers \nWelfare (Department of Agriculture, Cooperation and Farmers Welfare) \nNotification No. S.O. 45 (E), dated the 4th January, 2019, including certain \nsubstances specified in the Schedule to the Insecticides Act, 1968, under \nsubsection (e) (ii) of Section 3 of the Insecticides Act, 1968.\n[Placed in Library. See No. L.T. 10784/16/19]\nII. (1) A copy each (in English and Hindi) of the following papers, under \nsub-section (1) (b) of Section 394 of the Companies Act, 2013:—\n(a) Fifty-fifth Annual Report and Accounts of the National Seeds \nCorporation (NSC) Limited, New Delhi, for the year 2017-18, together \nwith the Auditor’s Report on the Accounts and the comments of \nthe Comptroller and Auditor General of India thereon.\n(b) Review by Government on the working of the above Corporation.\n(2) Statement giving reasons for the delay in laying the papers mentioned \nat (1) above. [Placed in Library. See No. L.T. 10922/16/19]\nNotification of the Ministry of Chemicals and Fertilizers\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT \nAND HIGHWAYS; THE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF SHIPPING; \nAND THE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF CHEMICALS AND \nFERTILIZERS (SHRI MANSUKH MANDA VIYA): Sir, I lay on the Table, under \nsub-section (6) of Section 3 of the Essential Commodities Act, 1955, a copy (in \nEnglish and Hindi) of the Ministry of Chemicals and Fertilizers (Department of \nPharmaceuticals) Notification No. S.O. 39 (E), dated the 3rd January, 2019, publishing \nthe Drugs (Prices Control) Amendment Order, 2019.\n[Placed in Library. See No. L.T. 10786/16/19]\nI. Notification of the Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare\nII. Report and Accounts (2017-18) of NIAM, Jaipur and related papers\nSHRI PARSHOTTAM RUPALA: Sir, I lay on the Table, the following papers:–\nI. A copy (in English and Hindi) of the Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers \nWelfare (Department of Agriculture, Cooperation and Farmers Welfare) \n\n6 Information to [RAJYA SABHA] the House\nNotification No. G.S.R. 1167 (E), dated the 4th December, 2018, publishing \nthe Bhagar Grading and Marking Rules, 2018, under sub-section (3) of \nSection 3 of the Agricultural Produce (Grading and Marking) Act, 1937.\n[Placed in Library. See No. L.T. 11030/16/19]\nII. A copy each (in English and Hindi) of the following papers:—\n(a) Annual Report and Accounts of Ch. Charan Singh National Institute of \nAgricultural Marketing (NIAM), Jaipur, for the year 2017-18, together \nwith the Auditor’s Report on the Accounts.\n(b) Performance Review of the above Institute, for the year 2017-18.\n(c) Statement giving reasons for the delay in laying the papers mentioned \nat (a) above. [Placed in Library. See No. L.T. 11031/16/19]\n————\nREPORT OF THE COMMITTEE ON PAPERS LAID ON THE TABLE\nDR. C.P. THAKUR (Bihar): Sir, I present the 156th Report (in English and Hindi) \nof the Committee on Papers Laid on the Table, Rajya Sabha on ‘Delayed Laying \nof Annual Reports and Audited Accounts of Central Adoption Resource Authority \n(CARA) and Mahanagar Telephone Nigam Limited (MTNL)’.\n————\nINFORMATION TO THE HOUSE\nMR. CHAIRMAN: Now, Shri Prakash Javadekar.\nTHE MINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT (SHRI PRAKASH \nJA V ADEKAR): Sir, an important issue has come up over the last two three days \nwhich had people agitated as to how reservation works in the University. I have \nlistened to everyone’s opinon. Today, I want to tell this House that the Government \nis always in favour of social justice. We have decided to bring ordinance or bill, \nwhichever, in case of dismissal of review petition. ...(Interruptions)... one minute, \n...(Interruptions)... and secondly ...(Interruptions)...\nMR. CHAIRMAN: What is this? You need not answer them ...(Interruptions)... \nPlease sit down. ...(Interruptions)... I am not going to allow this to happen.\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF PARLIAMENTARY \nAFFAIRS AND THE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF STATISTICS \nAND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION (SHRI VIJAY GOEL): This is what you \nwere demanding. ...(Interruptions)...\n\nInformation to [8 February, 2019] the House 7\nSHRI PRAKASH JA V ADEKAR: The Government in already working on your \ndemands. ...(Interruptions)... the debate on ...(Interruptions)... SLP in the Supreme \nCourt. ...(Interruptions)...\nMR. CHAIRMAN: Now, Zero Hour ...(Interruptions)... What is this?\nSHRI PRAKASH JA V ADEKAR: I lay it before the House as well because \nit is important as to how much has been represented. We have conducted a new \nstudy. We did a case study of 30 Universities under this and found that if we do it \ndepartment-wise now then how it becouses unfair to the Scheduled Castes, Scheduled \nTribes and OBCs. We have analysed it completely. In case the review petition is not \napproved, the Government has the option of ordinance or Bill open ...(Interruptions)... \nuntil then this recruitment will not take place anywhere, we will ensure that too.\nMR. CHAIRMAN: Now your main issue and the issue that you had raised \nsubsequently, both have been resolved. ...(Interruptions)...\nSHRI NEERAJ SHEKHAR (Uttart Pradesh): Sir, what we have got this \n...(Interruptions)... What is this? ...(Interruptions)... Who is the thief?\nMR. CHAIRMAN: Who has given that? ...(Interruptions)...\nSHRI NEERAJ SHEKHAR: Sir, it was on my seat. ...(Interruptions)... Who is \nthe thief? ...(Interruptions)...\nMR. CHAIRMAN: If a mad person has done this, then it is wrong. \n...(Interruptions)... How can anybody distribute pamphlets in the House? How can \nanybody distribute pamphlets? This is disrespect to the House. We will order an \nenquiry. Secretary General, you order an enquiry and then find out.\nSHRI NEERAJ SHEKHAR: Sir, am I supposed to read this? ...(Interruptions)...\nMR. CHAIRMAN: We will order an inquiry; the Secretary-General to order an \ninquiry and then find out.\nHon. Members, I have received notices under Rule 267; Professor Manoj Kumar \nJha’s notice with regard to roster has been settled, along with Shrimati Misha Bharti’s; \nthen Shri D. Raja’s notice is about the same issue; Shri Ravi Prakash Verma’s notice \nis about the same issue; Shri Javed Ali Khan’s notice too is about the same issue; \nShri Ashok Siddharth’s notice is about the same issue; Shri Sanjay Singh’s notice is \nabout the same issue. This issue has already been discussed and answered.\nOn Shri Elamaram Kareem’s notice about alleged intervention by PMO in Rafale \ndeal; Shri Anand Sharma’s demand for JPC investigation into alleged irregularities/ \n\n8 Information to [RAJYA SABHA] the House\ncorruption in Rafale deal, I have disallowed them. You have a great opportunity to \ndiscuss all these issues in detail and question ...(Interruptions)... Please sit down. \nAnd you can demand answers from the Government during the discussion on the \nPresident’s Address to the House. That is a larger opportunity given to all of you. \nWe have already lost so much of time. We are left with only three more days. I \nappeal to all the Members once again to please allow the House to function and \nthen discuss these issues in the President’s Address. That is my advice to all of \nyou. ...(Interruptions)...\n†THE LEADER OF OPPOSITION (SHRI GHULAM NABI AZAD): Hon. \nChairman, Sir, my fellow has also given Notice ...(Interruptions)...\nMR. CHAIRMAN: I am not allowing an issue which has been disallowed by \nme. ...(Interruptions)... The LoP is aware of the rules. You are aware of the rules.\nSHRI GHULAM NABI AZAD: Sir, today such an issue has come out. \n...(Interruptions)... it is in the newspaper in Hindu ...(Interruptions)...\nMR. CHAIRMAN: This will not go on record. ...(Interruptions)...\nSHRI ANAND SHARMA (Himachal Pradesh): *\nSHRI DEREK O’BRIEN (West Bengal): *\nMR. CHAIRMAN: This will not go on record. A notice which is disallowed \nby the Chairman can’t be raised in the House, please. ...(Interruptions)... This will \nnot go on record. ...(Interruptions)...\nSHRI B. K. HARIPRASAD (Karnataka): *\nMR. CHAIRMAN: Nothing shall go on record. ...(Interruptions)... Nothing shall go \non record. Anything else I would have allowed. But, on the notice disallowed by the \nChair, nobody can speak on that. ...(Interruptions)... What is this? ...(Interruptions)...\nThe House is adjourned to meet at 11.00 a.m. on Monday, the 11th February, \n2019.\nThe House then adjourned at seven minutes past \neleven of the clock till eleven of the clock on \nMonday, the 11th February, 2019.\n† The speech delivered by the Hon. member in Urdu is available in the floor version.\n* Not recorded.\n[Mr. Chairman]\n\nPublished  under  r ule  260 of  r ules  of  Procedure  and  c onduct  of  b usiness  in \nthe  c ouncil  of  sta tes (r ajy a sabha ) and  Printed  by  DRV Grafix  Print\n41, institutional  a rea , d -b lock , janak Puri , n ew  d elhi -110058",
